<title>ITALY: Italy offers 15.0 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</title>
<headline>Italy offers 15.0 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian treasury said it was offering 15.0 trillion lire of short term bills (BOT), replacing 17.25 trillion lire of expiring paper.</p>
<p>A Treasury statement said it would offer:</p>
<p>* 3.5 trillion lire of three-month BOTs</p>
<p>* 5.0 trillion lire of six-month paper</p>
<p>* 6.5 trillion lire of one-year bills.</p>
<p>Subscriptions close at 1200 GMT on November 12.</p>
<p>The treasury added that it would offer 2.5 trillion lire of two-year zero couponed certificates (CTZ) with subscriptions for that sale also closing at 1200 GMT, November 12.</p>
</text>
